From 5cbca9d2505eeeba3bc7ad39b35faa82f053e624 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:01:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] turnip (Doris): measure SYSMEM vs GMEM for Eden's render
 passes; report where the GPU time goes

- driconf: for the engine "yuzu Emulator" (Eden), tu_autotune_algorithm=profiled: each render pass
  with 5 or more draws is timed on the GPU in both modes and the faster one is used (locked once it
  is clearly faster), instead of the bandwidth estimate.
- autotune: when the process is Eden, every 10 seconds append to <app files>/log/apex_doris.txt
  the GPU time of the timed render passes per second (SYSMEM and GMEM, binning), and the render
  passes that took the most, with their size, draws, both modes' averages and the current choice;
  the whole session every minute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
